# LeRobot / SO-101 / LeKiwi — agent guidance

This repo is a **simulation-first** LeRobot workspace for learning robotics with the
SO-101 and LeKiwi ecosystem. No robot hardware is assumed connected.

## Read this first (mandatory)

Before suggesting robot, training, recording, or calibration commands, follow:

https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/blob/main/AGENT_GUIDE.md

Local copy after setup: `lerobot/AGENT_GUIDE.md`

Repo architecture map: `docs/architecture.md`

That guide requires asking about goal, hardware, GPU, skill level, dataset, and
the concrete next step — then picking the simplest path that fits.

## Install / activate

```bash
# First time (or recreate)
bash scripts/setup_lerobot.sh

# Every shell
source lerobot/.venv/bin/activate
# Stay at repo root so `python -m learning.smoke` resolves
```

Official install docs: https://huggingface.co/docs/lerobot/installation

## Constraints for this workspace

- Prefer simulation (`pusht`, Hub datasets, `lerobot-eval`, `python -m learning.smoke`) until hardware is available.
- Do **not** assume USB ports, cameras, or motors are connected.
- This machine may be CPU-only; use `--policy.device=cpu` (or `mps` on Apple Silicon) unless CUDA is verified via `lerobot-info` / `learning.smoke`.
- Feetech / SO-101 / LeKiwi extras are installed for later; skip `lerobot-find-port`, calibrate, record, and rollout until hardware is present.
- Do not vendor or rewrite upstream `lerobot/` in this git repo (`lerobot/` is gitignored). Prefer thin helpers under `learning/` and setup scripts under `scripts/`.
